🚀 DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 12

Kubernetes (Basics + Advanced) | 0–2 Years Experience

Kubernetes is the heart of cloud-native DevOps.
Interviewers don’t expect mastery — but they do expect you to understand how applications actually run in Kubernetes.

📌 Focus: Kubernetes Interview Questions (Basics + Advanced)

• What is Kubernetes and why is it used?
• Kubernetes architecture (master vs worker nodes)
• What is a cluster?
• What is a Pod?
• Pod vs container
• What is a Deployment?
• Deployment vs StatefulSet vs DaemonSet
• What is a ReplicaSet?
• What is a Service in Kubernetes?
• Service types (ClusterIP, NodePort, LoadBalancer)
• What is Ingress?
• Ingress vs LoadBalancer service
• What is ConfigMap?
• What is Secret?
• How do you store sensitive data in Kubernetes?
• What is Namespace?
• Why are namespaces used?
• What is a label and selector?
🔹 Advanced Kubernetes Concepts (Beginner-Friendly)

• What is HPA (Horizontal Pod Autoscaler)?
• How does auto-scaling work in Kubernetes?
• What is liveness and readiness probe?
• Difference between liveness and readiness probe
• What is resource request and limit?
• What happens when a pod exceeds memory limit?
• What is rolling update?
• Rolling update vs recreate strategy
• What is Helm?
• Why is Helm used?
• What is CRD (Custom Resource Definition)?
• What is RBAC?
• Role vs ClusterRole
• How do you secure a Kubernetes cluster?
• How do you troubleshoot a failing pod?
• Common Kubernetes mistakes beginners make
• Real-world Kubernetes deployment flow

Interview Tip:
If you can explain:
👉 “Docker image → Deployment → Service → Ingress → Scale”
you already sound like a real Kubernetes DevOps engineer, even with 0–2 years of experience.
